 a Python function to find the k-th smallest value in a list of integers, using only the standard library. This implementation uses a selection algorithm based on quicksort's partitioning logic to achieve an average time complexity of O(n).

```python
def solve(nums, k):
    def partition(left, right, pivot_idx):
        pivot_val = nums[pivot_idx]
        nums[pivot_idx], nums[right] = nums[right], nums[pivot_idx]
        store_idx = left
        for i in range(left, right):
            if nums[i] < pivot_val:
                nums[store_idx], nums[i] = nums[i], nums[store_idx]
                store_idx += 1
        nums[right], nums[store_idx] = nums[store_idx], nums[right]
        return store_idx

    def select(left, right, k):
        if left == right:
            return nums[left]
        pivot_idx = left + (right - left) // 2
        pivot_idx = partition(left, right, pivot_idx)
        if k == pivot_idx - left + 1:
            return nums[pivot_idx]
        elif k < pivot_idx - left + 1:
            return select(left, pivot_idx - 1, k)
        else:
            return select(pivot_idx + 1, right, k - (pivot_idx - left + 1))

    return select(0, len(nums) - 1, k)
```

